RabbitVCS Dolphin VCS plugin
============================

Native Dolphin version-control plugin that integrates RabbitVCS into
Dolphin. It shows the Git/Subversion status of files and adds a
"RabbitVCS Git" / "RabbitVCS SVN" submenu to Dolphin's context menu.

This project is independent of the RabbitVCS source tree; it only needs
the RabbitVCS runtime installed on the system.


Requirements
------------

    * Dolphin 6 (with its libdolphinvcs development files), KIO 6 and Qt 6
    * CMake 3.20+, Extra CMake Modules (ECM), KF6CoreAddons and KF6KIO
    * the RabbitVCS runtime (the `rabbitvcs` command, e.g. the
      `rabbitvcs-cli` package) in PATH
    * `git` and/or `svn` for the status overlays; `git` is also needed to
      run the tests


Package install
---------------

Packaging recipes live in packaging/ (Ubuntu 26.04, Fedora, Arch Linux; see
packaging/README.md). Ubuntu 24.04 is not supported: it has no KDE
Frameworks 6.


Build and install
-----------------

    ./scripts/build.sh
    ./scripts/install.sh

Both use /usr as the installation prefix by default. Override it with the
PREFIX environment variable, for example:

    PREFIX=$HOME/.local ./scripts/install.sh

Remove the installed files with:

    ./scripts/uninstall.sh

The plugins are installed into <prefix>/lib/qt6/plugins/dolphin/vcs on a
system prefix; a private prefix is supported as well, in which case Qt needs
to find it through QT_PLUGIN_PATH.


Development
-----------

CMake presets are provided (see CMakePresets.json):

    cmake --workflow --preset test       # debug build and unit tests
    cmake --workflow --preset release    # release build
    cmake --workflow --preset package-deb    # release build + .deb (CPack)
    cmake --workflow --preset package-rpm    # release build + .rpm (CPack)

The CPack packages are written to build/. They use the install layout of the
machine that builds them (Debian multiarch lib dirs, Fedora lib64), so build
the .deb on Debian/Ubuntu and the .rpm on Fedora.

Layout:

    src/        plugin code and the two plugin metadata files
    tests/      Qt Test unit tests
    scripts/    build / install / uninstall helpers
    packaging/  distribution packaging recipes

CI (.github/workflows/ci.yml) runs the test and release workflows, and builds
the .deb (Ubuntu 26.04) and .rpm (Fedora) as downloadable artifacts, on every
push and pull request.


Enable in Dolphin
-----------------

    Settings -> Configure Dolphin... -> Context Menu

Tick "RabbitVCS Git" and/or "RabbitVCS SVN". New version-control plugins are
disabled by default.

Do not enable the stock "Git" or "Subversion" plugin at the same time:
Dolphin picks the first enabled plugin whose marker file (.git / .svn)
matches, so two plugins for the same VCS would compete with each other.


